[b]Single player only. Build 42.[/b]

Cloth face coverings, and gas masks or respirators with a filter fitted, cut the sickness you get from nearby corpses and zombies by at least 50%. In vanilla, bandanas, shemaghs, dust masks and surgical masks give 25%.

What gets raised to the minimum:
[list]
[*]Anything that already has some corpse sickness protection, vanilla or modded.
[*]Cloth worn on the face: cotton or denim items, or anything named balaclava, bandana, shemagh, scarf, gaiter or head sack.
[*]Gas masks and respirators with a spent filter. With a good filter they keep their full vanilla value, and with no filter they keep their own vanilla value.
[/list]
Items that already protect more keep their own value. Hockey, Halloween, bone and welding masks, full helmets, neck scarves and bandanas worn on the head are left alone.

[h2]Options[/h2]
Sandbox page "Face Mask Protection": Minimum protection (%), 0 to 100, default 50. Set it to 0 to leave every item at its original value.

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*]Can be added to an existing save.
[*]Cloth face masks from other mods are covered by the rules above, no patch needed.
[*]Single player only.
[/list]

[h2]Known issues[/h2]
[list]
[*]Filters are checked every game minute and when your clothing changes, so pulling a filter out can take up to a minute to count.
[*]Head sacks made of garbage bag, tarp or hide count as cloth because of their name.
[/list]

Source and bug reports: [url=https://github.com/maxcwolf/pz-mods/tree/main/face-covering-protection]GitHub[/url]
